# DEBT-0006 — Consolidate `SealAuthority` Index Under `Projector[SealRecord]`

**Status**: OPEN  
**Filed**: 2026-07-28  
**Priority**: Low  
**Category**: Code Refactoring / TCB DRY Enforcement  

---

## 1. Compromise
`SealAuthority` in [kernel/seal.py](file:///Users/bob/GitHub/paeos/kernel/seal.py) implements its own in-memory index rebuild loop (`_rebuild_index`) by iterating directly over ledger rows at startup.

## 2. Reason
Task **B0.9 (Seal Authority)** was implemented prior to Task **B0.10 (Projections & Replay Engine)**. `kernel/projections.py` now provides the canonical, generic `Projector[S]` fold pattern over the ledger.

## 3. Ideal Solution
Refactor `SealAuthority`'s index initialization to consume `kernel/projections.py`'s `Projector[SealIndexState]` fold pattern rather than maintaining a custom ledger scan loop.

## 4. Repayment Conditions
Repay during post-Phase 0 kernel refactoring or during Phase 1 projection expansion.

## 5. Estimated Impact
Low operational impact (`SealAuthority` passes all 13 unit/restart tests today). Eliminates ~30 lines of redundant ledger scanning logic in the TCB.
